+<section class="section-sand" id="faq">
+  <div class="container">
+    <div class="section-head left" style="max-width:720px; margin-left:auto; margin-right:auto;">
+      <span class="eyebrow">Frequently Asked</span>
+      <h2>10 Days to 2 Weeks in Morocco: Quick Answers</h2>
+    </div>
+    <div class="article-body">
+      <div class="faq-category">
+        <details class="faq-item">
+          <summary>Is 10 days enough to see Morocco?</summary>
+          <p>Ten days is the length we recommend most for a first visit. It's enough to see Chefchaouen, Fes, the Sahara and Marrakech at a comfortable pace, with two nights in the desert and free time in the cities. You'll still leave the Atlantic coast and the far south for another trip, or for a two-week itinerary.</p>
+        </details>
+        <details class="faq-item">
+          <summary>What should a 10-day Morocco itinerary include?</summary>
+          <p>A balanced 10-day itinerary usually includes a guided day in Fes, a night in Chefchaouen, the Roman ruins of Volubilis, two nights in the Sahara at Merzouga, the Todra Gorges and Dades Valley, Ait Benhaddou and two nights in Marrakech.</p>
+        </details>
+        <details class="faq-item">
+          <summary>How should I spend 2 weeks in Morocco?</summary>
+          <p>Two weeks lets you add the Atlantic coast and slow down. A popular 13-14 day route adds two nights in Essaouira, a second night in Chefchaouen or the Atlas Mountains, and a remote desert such as Erg Chigaga. Our 13-day grand loop from Casablanca is a good starting point.</p>
+        </details>
+        <details class="faq-item">
+          <summary>How much does a 10-day private tour of Morocco cost?</summary>
+          <p>Our 9 to 11-day private journeys cost roughly €1,775 to €2,400 per person for two people sharing, and our 10-day Ultimate Desert Journey from Marrakech costs from €2,045. Prices include your driver-guide and vehicle, accommodation, breakfasts, desert dinners and the camel trek.</p>
+        </details>
+        <details class="faq-item">
+          <summary>Is it better to start a Morocco trip in Casablanca or Marrakech?</summary>
+          <p>For a 10-day loop that includes the north, starting in Casablanca and finishing in Marrakech (or the reverse) avoids backtracking. Casablanca often has the most convenient flights from North America; Marrakech has more connections through Europe.</p>
+        </details>
+      </div>
+    </div>
+  </div>
