+<div class="answer-box">
+        <p><strong>The short answer:</strong> Yes, Morocco is a safe destination for most tourists. The US State Department rates it <strong>Level 2, &ldquo;Exercise increased caution&rdquo;</strong>, the same level it gives many popular European countries, and Canada advises a <strong>&ldquo;high degree of caution&rdquo;</strong>. Both cite a general risk of terrorism. The problems most visitors actually meet are smaller ones: persistent selling, unofficial guides, petty theft in crowds and chaotic traffic. A little preparation, and ideally a trusted local guide, deals with nearly all of them.</p>
