+<section class="section-sand" id="faq">
+  <div class="container">
+    <div class="section-head left" style="max-width:720px; margin-left:auto; margin-right:auto;">
+      <span class="eyebrow">Frequently Asked</span>
+      <h2>Morocco for Couples: Quick Answers</h2>
+    </div>
+    <div class="article-body">
+      <div class="faq-category">
+        <details class="faq-item">
+          <summary>Is Morocco a good honeymoon destination?</summary>
+          <p>Yes. Morocco combines intimate riads, private desert camps, hammams, rooftop dinners and spectacular landscapes within a manageable distance, and it feels far more adventurous than a beach resort. It suits couples who want romance and discovery in the same trip.</p>
+        </details>
+        <details class="faq-item">
+          <summary>How many days do you need for a Morocco honeymoon?</summary>
+          <p>Eight to twelve days is ideal. That allows three nights in Marrakech, two nights in the Sahara and a slower final stop such as Essaouira or the Atlas Mountains, without long driving days back to back.</p>
+        </details>
+        <details class="faq-item">
+          <summary>What is the most romantic thing to do in Morocco?</summary>
+          <p>For most couples, it's a night or two at a luxury camp in the Sahara: a camel ride over the dunes at sunset, dinner by lantern light and a sky full of stars. A sunrise hot-air balloon flight over Marrakech and a private rooftop dinner in the medina come close behind.</p>
+        </details>
+        <details class="faq-item">
+          <summary>Can unmarried couples share a room in Morocco?</summary>
+          <p>Foreign couples, married or not, can share a room in hotels and riads without any problem. Moroccan law requires couples where one partner is Moroccan to show a marriage certificate to share a room.</p>
+        </details>
+        <details class="faq-item">
+          <summary>When is the best time for a honeymoon in Morocco?</summary>
+          <p>March to May and late September to November offer the best weather across the cities, mountains and desert. Winter is also lovely for couples, with sunny days and cozy evenings by the fire, but desert nights are cold.</p>
+        </details>
+      </div>
+    </div>
